  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 5023.02 Operator Requirements.\n\n(a) For each electrical display firing, the operator shall comply with the following:\n\n(1) All firing shall be done from a remote central control location that provides the operator(s) with an unobstructed view of the entire display;\n\n(2) All wiring and firing system set-up shall be done under the direct control of the operator who shall also insure that the firing device or control panel is properly safeguarded; and\n\n(3) Prior to the display, precautions shall be taken to preclude the possibility of premature ignition due to stray sources of electrical or radio frequency energy.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at Chapter Heading for Saf-C 5000) #6055, eff 7-1-95; amd by #7481, eff 4-25-01; paragraphs (a)(2)-(3) EXPIRED: 7-1-03; amd by #8117, INTERIM, eff 7-14-04; paragraphs (a)(2)-(3) EXPIRED: 1-10-05; amd by #8261, eff 1-21-05; amd by #9471, INTERIM, eff 5-15-09, EXPIRED: 11-11-09\n\nNew. #9765-A, eff 8-2-10; ss by #12738, eff 4-30-19",
